:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=ADDEXITPGM.Add Exit Program (ADDEXITPGM)
:P.Use the Add Exit Program (ADDEXITPGM) command to register a program
on an exit point and format.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDEXITPGM/EXITPNT'.Exit point (EXITPNT)
:P.The exit point, by name.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 20 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDEXITPGM/FORMAT'.Exit point format (FORMAT)
:P.The exit point format for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDEXITPGM/PGMNBR'.Program number (PGMNBR)
:P.The program number for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LOW:EPK.
:PD.Low.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 2147483647.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDEXITPGM/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDEXITPGM/THDSAFE'.Threadsafe (THDSAFE)
:P.The threadsafe for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *UNKNOWN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDEXITPGM/MLTTHDACN'.Multithreaded job action (MLTTHDACN)
:P.The multithreaded job action for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RUN, *NORUN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDEXITPGM/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDEXITPGM/REPLACE'.Replace an existing program (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDEXITPGM/CRTEXITPNT'.Create the exit point (CRTEXITPNT)
:P.Whether to create the exit point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDEXITPGM/PGMDTA'.Exit program data (PGMDTA)
:P.The exit program data for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Coded character set ID
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Length of data
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 2048.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Program data
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2048 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVEXITPGM.Remove Exit Program (RMVEXITPGM)
:P.Use the Remove Exit Program (RMVEXITPGM) command to take a program
off an exit point and format.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVEXITPGM/EXITPNT'.Exit point (EXITPNT)
:P.The exit point, by name.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 20 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVEXITPGM/FORMAT'.Exit point format (FORMAT)
:P.The exit point format for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVEXITPGM/PGMNBR'.Program number (PGMNBR)
:P.The program number for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 2147483647.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKREGINF.Work with Registration Info (WRKREGINF)
:P.Use the Work with Registration Info (WRKREGINF) command to list the
exit points and work with their programs.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKREGINF/EXITPNT'.Exit point (EXITPNT)
:P.The exit point, by name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 20 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REGISTERED, *UNREGISTERED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKREGINF/FORMAT'.Exit point format (FORMAT)
:P.The exit point format for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKREGINF/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
